WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.060
Not every chilling horror scene makes it to
the big screen.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.080
Whether for pacing reasons, keeping the MPAA
rating at an accessible "R," or simply the

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.429
filmmakers going in a different direction,
these scenes were left on the cutting room

00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:13.740
floor — but they're no less terrifying on
their own.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.280
Here are some of the scariest deleted scenes
from your favorite horror movies.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.420
But beware...the spoilers!

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:20.900
The cocoon room

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.020
There were a lot of ideas that never came
to fruition in Ridley Scott's Alien, but what

00:00:25.021 --> 00:00:29.660
we were left with was still a groundbreaking
extraterrestrial thriller — often imitated,

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:30.640
never quite matched.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.850
The plot follows a commercial space crew awoken
from stasis after receiving a signal from

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:35.640
an alien craft.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:40.559
They're overrun by the bloodthirsty extra-terrestrial
monster, with Officer Ripley emerging as the

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.360
central heroine and only survivor.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.440
One of the deleted scenes from the film might've
answered a few questions left about the alien

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.000
— and escalated the fear factor.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.460
In this cocoon room scene, Ripley happens
upon the trapped bodies of the deceased Brett

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:56.440
and the still-alive Dallas, whose whereabouts
were otherwise unknown after they ran into

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.820
the creature in the original cut.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:03.140
As an act of mercy, Ripley has to fire-blast
Dallas, which is pretty raw, even for Alien.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.100
The baboon cat

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.820
The Fly is a seminal piece of horror, with
or without its scariest deleted scene.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.680
The sci-fi thriller followed Seth Brundle
as he became a victim of his own oddball scientific

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:15.180
experiments.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:20.080
He slowly morphed into a human-fly hybrid
that was desperate to save his new species...by

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.240
making a baby with his human girlfriend.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:25.560
In this deleted scene, even though Brundle's
teleportation experience has clearly altered

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:28.780
his own DNA, he's still splicing animals together
in his lab.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.220
This time, it's a baboon and a house cat,
which when combined becomes a two-headed,

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:36.580
sharp-toothed beast that goes on the attack
and has to be exterminated.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:41.259
It might've been a bit too obvious as foreshadowing
if left in, but the scene definitely doesn't

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:44.640
offer much hope for Brundle's own future as
a fellow lab mutant.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:45.720
"I'm scared."

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.020
Uh, yeah.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:48.760
Visions of Hell

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.900
Event Horizon is filled with stomach-churning
imagery.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.950
The movie followed a space crew as they attempted
to make contact with a vessel that was temporarily

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:00.259
lost to a black hole, and layered itself with
disturbing visuals before jumping headlong

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.220
into a living nightmare.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:05.280
But as sinister as the scenes of this space
inferno already are, the movie's original

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:08.160
vision of the bad place was even more disturbing.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.200
"A dimension of pure chaos.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.400
Pure evil."

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:18.120
In this deleted scene, Dr. William Weir has
been fully transformed into the slash-faced

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:22.260
demon that haunts the ship and its remaining
crew, and Captain Miller is chased down and

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.180
treated to an extreme vision of the other
side.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.960
Impaled, limb-ripped bodies are on display
as the living are tied down and tortured.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:33.129
The plights of these human souls may differ
slightly, but the suffering is universal.

00:02:33.129 --> 00:02:36.640
Given the graphic nature of this footage,
it's not hard to see why an abbreviated version

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.680
was ultimately what made it into theaters.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:42.440
Even Dante might've shuddered at the sight
of this much underworldly punishment.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.340
Dr. Satan's last lunge

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:49.060
With The Devil's Rejects, writer-director
Rob Zombie took a decidedly different approach

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:52.780
to the macabre than he did with its predecessor,
House of 1000 Corpses.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:56.340
Rather than relying on gruesome imagery in
the loathsome lair of the Firefly family,

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:00.819
the movie leaned harder on a slow burn of
emotional torture and depravity as it followed

00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:04.110
the three lead escapees through one final
round of destruction.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:06.730
For that reason, this deleted scene wasn't
a good fit.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:08.520
In the clip, we meet Dr. Satan again.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:12.600
The character's twisted experimental surgeries
featured prominently in the first film, and

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.440
in Rejects he's been captured by the authorities.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:16.720
But he isn't as subdued as they think.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:21.060
His unsuspecting nurse gets her throat ripped
out after he awakens from his feigned coma,

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:25.240
and the move is so quick that the police and
medical personnel can do nothing to stop her

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:26.940
from bleeding out on the hospital floor.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:28.500
The tilted room

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:33.450
The adaptation of Stephen King's 1408 follows
skeptical haunted house story author as he

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.250
rents out a deadly hotel room that's claimed
the lives of dozens of occupants over the

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:37.840
last century.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:42.380
What happens next is a bit formulaic, but
is bolstered by sensory immersion with enough

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.960
paranormal surprises and emotional scenes
to stick.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.391
In this deleted scene, Jon Cusack's estranged
wife has been summoned to the hotel by his

00:03:49.391 --> 00:03:53.420
supernatural doppelgänger, and he's powerless
to stop her from trying to enter the room.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:57.209
As he tries to get close to prevent her from
joining him, the room tilts to a degree that

00:03:57.209 --> 00:03:58.840
disables him from reaching the door.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:03.700
For all the elemental frights the room provided,
this had to be the most disorienting, despite

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.260
being deleted.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.560
The final cut

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.290
The theatrically released ending of Paranormal
Activity was pretty upsetting.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:13.370
In the film, Katie and Micah are a young couple
who've moved to the wrong house at the wrong

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:16.340
time and can't shake the terrorizing spirits
that came with it.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:20.420
Despite their best efforts to exorcise the
evil spirits from their home, Katie is eventually

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:24.949
possessed by the demon spirit, and appears
to end Micah by summoning him downstairs and

00:04:24.949 --> 00:04:28.900
then hurling his bloody body at the camera
they'd been using to document their haunting.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:33.190
She then shuffles onscreen, looks at the camera,
and offers a smile that makes it clear she's

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.520
given herself over to evil.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:38.580
In the original ending, though, Katie returns
to the bedroom in what appears to be a trance

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.770
and sits rocking on the floor as time passes.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:44.910
Eventually, the police show up, find Micah's
body, and make their way upstairs to Katie.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:48.420
She snaps out of her trance, but police believe
she's a threat and shoot her.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:52.580
The scariest version, though, is the alternate
ending, when instead of launching Micah's

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:56.350
body at the camera, she returns to the frame
herself, covered in blood and holding her

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.520
kitchen knife which she then uses on herself.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:02.280
Chance are this one was passed over because
it would've ended the hit franchise before

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.220
it began, but still.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:04.320
What a way to go.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:05.280
Thanks for watching!

